ecialty, the backstroke, leading by over 1½ seconds at 200 metres. Sanders went ahead again at the end of the breaststroke, as Lin closed on the duo. But Egerszegi had the most left. She took the lead just before the final turn and held it on the last lap to win the gold medal in 4:36.54. Lin also passed Sanders, finishing in 4:36.73, as Sanders’ bronze medal winning time of 4:37.58 was still six seconds ahead of fourth-placed Australian " [:a {:href "/athletes/45075"} "Hayley Lewis"] ". The medal-winning times were the third, fourth, and fifth fastest performances of all-time, trailing only the world record from 1982 by East German " [:a {:href "/athletes/47531"} "Petra Schneider"] " (4:36.10) and her 1980 Olympic winning time of 4:36.29."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "331"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/48094"} "Krisztina Egerszegi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "4:43.83 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "4:36.54 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "112"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/46089"} "Lin Li"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} "4:45.74 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "4:36.73 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "628"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51177"} "Summer Sanders"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "pa